    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>Wondrous Item, Artifact (Requires Attunement)</em></p><p>Vecna was a mighty wizard who forged a terrible empire through magic and conquest. For all his power, he feared death and took steps to cheat it by becoming a lich.</p><p>A treacherous lieutenant named Kas ended Vecna’s rule in a terrible battle. All that remained of Vecna were one hand and one eye, grisly Artifacts that still seek to work his will in the world.</p><p>The <em>Eye of Vecna</em> and the <em>Hand of Vecna</em> are separate Artifacts that might be found together or apart. The eye looks like a bloodshot organ torn from its socket; the hand is a shriveled left hand.</p><p><strong>Random Properties.</strong> The <em>Eye of Vecna</em> and the <em>Hand of Vecna</em> each have the following random properties (see “Artifacts”):</p><ul><li><p>1 minor beneficial property</p></li><li><p>1 major beneficial property</p></li><li><p>1 minor detrimental property</p></li></ul><p><strong>Attuning to the Eye.</strong> To attune to the eye, you must press it into your empty eye socket. The eye grafts itself to your head and stays there until you die. If the eye is ever removed, you die.</p><p><strong>Properties of the Eye.</strong> While attuned to the eye, your alignment is Neutral Evil, and you gain the following benefits.</p><p><strong>Truesight.</strong> You have Truesight out to 240 feet.</p><p><strong>Spellcasting.</strong> The eye has 8 charges and regains 1d4 + 4 expended charges daily at dawn. You can cast a spell on the Eye of Vecna Spells table from the eye (save DC 18), expending the number of charges it shows. Each time you cast a spell from the eye, there is a 5 percent chance that Vecna tears your soul from your body, devours it, and takes control of your body like a puppet; you then become an NPC under the DM’s control.</p><p><strong>Eye of Vecna Spells</strong></p><table><thead><tr><th>Spell</th><th>Charge Cost</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplClairvoyan]{Clairvoyance}</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.compendium-owidyn.spells.Item.AYJBs5xqw7MrqMoD]{Crown of Madness}</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplDisintegra]{Disintegrate}</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplDominateMo]{Dominate Monster}</td><td>5</td></tr><tr><td>@UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplEyebite000]{Eyebite}</td><td>4</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>X-ray Vision.</strong> You can take a Magic action to gain X-ray vision with a range of 30 feet for 1 minute. To you, solid objects within that radius look transparent and don’t block light. The vision can see through 1 foot of stone, 1 inch of common metal, or up to 3 feet of wood or dirt; thicker substances block it, as does a thin sheet of lead.</p><p><strong>Properties of the Eye and Hand.</strong> While attuned to both the hand and the eye, you gain the following additional benefits.</p><p><strong>Danger Sense.</strong> You have Advantage on Initiative rolls.</p><p><strong>Necrotic Reduction.</strong> As a Magic action, you can target one creature you can see within 5 feet of yourself. It makes a DC 18 Constitution saving throw, taking 7d6 Necrotic damage on a failed save or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature reduced to 0 Hit Points by this damage becomes green slime covering the ground in its space, each 5-foot square of slime being a separate patch. Nonmagical objects of metal or organic material worn or carried by the target are destroyed by the slime.</p><p><strong>Poison Immunity.</strong> You have Immunity to Poison damage and the &amp;Reference[Poisoned apply=false] condition.</p><p><strong>Regeneration.</strong> If you start your turn with at least 1 Hit Point, you regain 1d10 Hit Points.</p><p><strong>Wish.</strong> You can cast @UUID[Compendium.dnd5e.spells24.Item.phbsplWish000000]{Wish}. Once used, this property can’t be used again until 30 days have passed.</p><p><strong>Destroying the Eye and Hand.</strong> If the eye and the hand are both attached to the same creature and that creature is slain by the @UUID[Compendium.compendium-owidyn.items.Item.JPSwohUl80C5s6Eu]{Sword of Kas}, both burst into flame, turn to ash, and are destroyed. Any other attempt to destroy the eye or the hand seems to work, but the Artifact reappears in one of Vecna’s many hidden vaults, where it waits to be found again.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-XmXPirpm8h61sMia\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p>Les propriétés aléatoires d’artefact sont à ajouter par le MJ. <em>Vecna’s Hunger</em> lance le d100 après chaque sort de l’œil (5 ou moins : Vecna prend le contrôle). Les propriétés communes à l’œil et à la main sont sur cet objet : si vous êtes harmonisé aux deux, activez l’effet <em>Eye and Hand of Vecna</em> et utilisez les activités <em>Necrotic Reduction</em>, <em>Regeneration</em> et <em>Wish</em> (rendez l’utilisation de <em>Wish</em> à la main au bout de 30 jours). <em>Crown of Madness</em> vient du compendium Spells.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
